{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Against You</b> — this is the sin that is against me always; it is that I have sinned against You alone." "And the meaning of <b>that You may be justified</b> — connect it with <b>my transgression I acknowledge</b>. The meaning: I confess and there is no need to reprove me. Or it may be connected with <b>be gracious to me</b>, for I confess, and You said that You will forgive the penitent who confess their iniquity."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:31.881924006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}